  "note": "Fixes real PR review findings from chatgpt-codex-connector[bot] and tenki-reviewer[bot]: missing Pillow/cryptography deps; signature verification did not check public-key fingerprint against recorded values; render scripts used an unbounded ffmpeg glob and did not reverify before encoding; verify_competition_lineage.py only checked field presence not equality against the ledger; qualified_breakpoint.py permitted a caller body to override identity fields (fixed directly, not a protected atom). Original verify/render scripts are protected atoms of BP-0011/0012 and were not edited in place; v2 files supersede them, writing to distinctly-named receipt files to avoid clobbering the protected originals (a mistake made and corrected during this same pass). README Tenki overclaim corrected to match the actual submission candidate (both sponsor flags false, matching operator-stated TENKI_FINAL_STATE=BLOCKED_INVALID_OR_REVOKED_API_KEY). A key-management gap (two playthroughs signed with two different locally-generated keys, no single published trust anchor) was found and documented rather than silently fixed given time constraints. Independently reverified: final canonical.mp4 sha256 d9f977296d42e414a4c1e1c9ccd2cc3d69a5f093fef10be4821781265c458a06 matches exactly.",
